.TH "TRCC\-DEVICE" "1" "" "trcc\-linux 9.9.11" "TRCC Manual"
.SH NAME
trcc\-device \- Discover and connect to TRCC devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrcc device\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Discover and connect to TRCC devices.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS connect
.PP
\fBtrcc device connect\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Open USB transport and perform the wire\-protocol handshake.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS disconnect
.PP
\fBtrcc device disconnect\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Close the transport and drop the device.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
(no description)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS issues
.PP
\fBtrcc device issues\fR
.PP
Show devices that failed to connect, and why. A connect can fail before anything is watching the bus, so the failure is pulled with a query rather than only published  \-  the same one the GUIs and GET /devices/issues use.
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS list
.PP
\fBtrcc device list\fR
.PP
List devices currently attached to the host.
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS reset
.PP
\fBtrcc device reset\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Disconnect + clear cached state for a device. Use this when the LCD seems stuck  \-  drops any cached frame, theme, and runtime counters. Re\-running connect after this starts completely fresh.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
(no description)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS state
.PP
\fBtrcc device state\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Show what a device IS  \-  identity, connection, handshake geometry. native_resolution is what the product registry claims; resolution is what the panel answered at handshake. When they differ, the handshake wins and the difference is usually the thing worth reporting.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtrcc\fR(1)
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report bugs at \fBhttps://github.com/Lexonight1/thermalright-trcc-linux/issues\fR \(em include the output of \fBtrcc report\fR.
.SH AUTHOR
TRCC Linux contributors. Unofficial community project, not affiliated with Thermalright.
